      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mayflower Village earned its name from the Mayflower School built in 1927, a landmark that early residents still remember.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_mayflower-village"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area began as San Gabriel Mission land, granted to settlers after Mexico secularized the missions in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_mayflower-village"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After World War II, former farmland was converted into a planned suburban community that defines Mayflower Village today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/mayflower-village-164671"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tree‑lined streets and historic bungalows from the 1920s give the village its distinct small‑town character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
